  "id": "COMPOUND:24022 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Miyabenol A appears to have a direct relationship with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a multi-tiered mechanism. The evidence suggests that Miyabenol A targets 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is then targeted by Diplotrin A. Diplotrin A, in turn, has a direct effect on Replicase polyprotein 1ab. This implies that Miyabenol A may act through a pathway involving the proteasome, with Diplotrin A serving as a mediator. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible link between Miyabenol A and Replicase polyprotein 1ab, though the exact mechanism by which Miyabenol A influences the proteasome or Diplotrin A remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential role for Miyabenol A in modulating the proteasome system, which could have implications for the regulation of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with the proteasome and Diplotrin A acting as key intermediaries.",
